* Class A 30 W combo, Normal / Brilliant channels (drawing "AC30 Standard Issue", 22/11/90): V4 (one
* 12AX7 triode per channel, shared cathode), the two volume pots, V5a gain stage, V5b cathode follower,
* the Treble / Bass tone network, and V6a (unbypassed cathode) driving the phase inverter.
* The Vib/Trem channel (V1..V3), the reverb (V6b, V7) and the footswitch are not modelled.
*
* Reading notes (the drawing is a hand-drawn low-resolution scan; change these here, not in code):
*  - V4's left triode is the Normal channel and the right one the Brilliant channel: separate grids behind
*    68k stoppers, separate 220k plate loads, one 1k5 / 22u cathode;
*  - Normal Vol takes 47n from its plate; Brilliant Vol takes 560p with a 100p bright cap across the pot;
*    both wipers meet at V5a's grid (through 100 ohm so the node names stay distinct);
*  - V5b's grid is V5a's plate; its cathode (68k) feeds the Treble / Bass network: 56p to the treble pot,
*    100k to the two 22n caps, bass pot between the treble pot's bottom and the 10k leg to ground;
*  - the Hi / Lo input pairs are modelled as the Hi input;
*  - supply: the preamp rail x is the power amp's HT3 (about 250 V); 10k + 33u steps to HT4 (180 V),
*    HT5 (160 V) and 4k7 + 33u to HT6 (135 V).

.nodes x n4 n5 n6 gin in jn jb g4a g4b p4a p4b k4 cn1 wn cb1 wb g5 p5a k5a k5b tt wt tu ta tb w2 g6 p6 k6 o

* HT3 (node x): driven from the power amp at run time; 250 V is the standalone default.
V VRAIL x 100 250
I VIN gin 1
R RSRC gin in 7k

* HT dropper chain.
R R_H4 x n4 10k
C C_H4 n4 0 33u
R R_H5 n4 n5 10k
C C_H5 n5 0 33u
R R_H6 n5 n6 4k7
C C_H6 n6 0 33u
* Stand-ins for the stages that are not modelled (Vib/Trem, reverb): they set the drawing's HT4 / HT5 / HT6 voltages.
R RL_H4 n4 0 120k
R RL_H5 n5 0 330k
R RL_H6 n6 0 120k

* Jacks. SW_* select the channel (closed 1 ohm / open 1e12), set by the jack modes.
R SW_N in jn 1
R R68_N jn g4a 68k
R RG_N g4a 0 1M
R SW_B in jb 1e12
R R68_B jb g4b 68k
R RG_B g4b 0 1M

* V4: Normal (A) and Brilliant (B) share the cathode network.
T V4A g4a p4a k4 12AX7
R R_P4A n6 p4a 220k
T V4B g4b p4b k4 12AX7
R R_P4B n6 p4b 220k
R RK4 k4 0 1k5
C CK4 k4 0 22u

* Volume pots (wiper = output).
C C47N p4a cn1 47n
R VR_NT cn1 wn 1
R VR_NB wn 0 1
C C560 p4b cb1 560p
R VR_BT cb1 wb 1
R VR_BB wb 0 1
C C100 cb1 wb 100p
R R_JN wn g5 100
R R_JB wb g5 100

* V5a gain stage and V5b cathode follower (grid on V5a's plate).
T V5A g5 p5a k5a 12AX7
R R_P5A n4 p5a 100k
R RK5 k5a 0 1k5
C CK5 k5a 0 22u
T V5B p5a n4 k5b 12AX7
R R68 k5b 0 68k

* Treble / Bass network.
C C56P k5b tt 56p
R VR_TT tt wt 1
R VR_TB wt tu 1
R R100K k5b ta 100k
C C22A ta tu 22n
C C22B ta tb 22n
R R10K tb 0 10k
R VR_KT tu tb 1
R VR_KB tb 0 1

* V6a: 220k + 10n from the treble wiper, 1M leak, 2k2 unbypassed cathode, 100k plate load on HT5.
R R220 wt w2 220k
C C10N w2 g6 10n
R R1M g6 0 1M
T V6A g6 p6 k6 12AX7
R R_P6 n5 p6 100k
R RK6 k6 0 2k2

* AC coupling to the phase inverter.
C C_OUT p6 o 100n
R R_O o 0 470k
